'''Tumeken's Guardian''' is a [[pet]] that can be obtained from completing the [[Tombs of Amascut]]. It is a much smaller version of [[Tumeken's Warden]]. Players have a chance of receiving the pet when looting the [[Chest (Tombs of Amascut)|reward chest]] in the burial chamber. It is possible for it to be obtained in Entry mode, although at a much lower rate.

When a player receives the pet, it will automatically try to appear as their follower. At the same time, a message in the [[Chat Interface|chatbox]] will state {{mes|You have a funny feeling like you're being followed.|color=red}} However, if a player receives a pet while having a follower out (for example, a [[cat]]), it will be placed into their [[inventory]]. When this occurs, the message in the chatbox will instead state {{mes|You feel something weird sneaking into your backpack.|color=red}}

If a player's inventory is full '''and''' they have a follower already, they '''will not''' receive the pet; it must instead be claimed from [[Probita]] in [[East Ardougne]].

On [[death]], if a player loses their pet (as a follower or in your inventory) it will wander around the area for 30 seconds before despawning. Even if the player returns in time, the pet cannot be picked up, and can be reclaimed from Probita.

==Metamorphosis==
Players can, by default, right click "''[[Metamorphosis]]"'' to change between Tumeken's Guardian and Elidinis' Guardian, a smaller version of [[Elidinis' Warden]].

Players can unlock further metamorphoses by acquiring various items, which are acquired from the reward chest after completing a raid whilst satisfying the following conditions; note that only one remnant can be obtained by the player per raid. If the requirements for multiple remnants are met, the following order of priority determines which one is awarded: Akkha, Zebak, Ba-Ba, Kephri, Ancient.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1683875076234522636|date=25 July 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/105942|archivedate=25 July 2023|quote=It's checking in this order: Akkha, Zebak, Baba, Kephri, Tumeken, Ancient.}}

* Raid Level at 450+
* Zero deaths for all party members
* All invocations for the specific boss enabled
* Path level must be at level 4+ (excluding the Wardens)

